{"id":"1ded503967fe2f50","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-trigonometric-sum.md","title":"Trigonometric Sum","display":"df-trigonometric-sum — Trigonometric Sum","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-trigonometric-sum","aliases":["58-df-trigonometric-sum","Trigonometric Sum"],"display":"df-trigonometric-sum — Trigonometric Sum","depends_on":["[[58-df-exponential]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-trigonometric-sum"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-trigonometric-sum</span><span>Trigonometric Sum</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-trigonometric-sum — Trigonometric Sum"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"689fa138a0ce2d6c\" href=\"?note=689fa138a0ce2d6c\" title=\"58-df-exponential\">58-df-exponential</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N \\in \\omega\">\\(N \\in \\omega\\)</span> (finite upper bound)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}\">\\(\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}\\)</span> (frequency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}\">\\(\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}\\)</span> is the uniquely specified complex exponential from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"689fa138a0ce2d6c\" href=\"?note=689fa138a0ce2d6c\" title=\"58-df-exponential\">58-df-exponential</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TrigSum}:\\omega\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C\">\\(\\operatorname{TrigSum}:\\omega\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C\\)</span> (finite trigonometric sum defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{DistToInteger}:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\">\\(\\operatorname{DistToInteger}:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\)</span> (distance to the nearest integer defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trigonometric\\text{-}sum} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{TrigSum}(N,\\alpha)\\coloneqq\\sum_{n=1}^{N}\\exp(2\\pi i\\alpha n)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trigonometric\\text{-}sum} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{TrigSum}(N,\\alpha)\\coloneqq\\sum_{n=1}^{N}\\exp(2\\pi i\\alpha n)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}distance\\text{-}to\\text{-}integer}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{DistToInteger}(\\alpha)\\coloneqq\\inf\\{|\\alpha-m|:m\\in\\mathbb Z\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}distance\\text{-}to\\text{-}integer}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{DistToInteger}(\\alpha)\\coloneqq\\inf\\{|\\alpha-m|:m\\in\\mathbb Z\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Trigonometric sum: finite sum of exponentials; fundamental in analytic number theory</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N=0\">\\(N=0\\)</span> the displayed finite sum is the empty sum, hence equals <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\">\\(0\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Gauss sums: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G(a, q) = \\sum_{n=1}^q e^{2\\pi i a n^2/q}\">\\(G(a, q) = \\sum_{n=1}^q e^{2\\pi i a n^2/q}\\)</span>; quadratic character sums</li>\n<li>The geometric-series identity, the bound in terms of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{DistToInteger}(\\alpha)\">\\(\\operatorname{DistToInteger}(\\alpha)\\)</span>, and Weyl's inequality are theorems about these sums, not additional definitions.</li>\n<li>Quantitative Weyl bounds depend on rational approximations to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\">\\(\\alpha\\)</span>; irrationality alone does not give a uniform <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N^{1/2+\\epsilon}\">\\(N^{1/2+\\epsilon}\\)</span> bound at every scale.</li>\n<li>Circle method: major/minor arc decomposition of trigonometric sums</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Vaughan, The Hardy-Littlewood Method</li>\n<li>Iwaniec, Topics in Classical Automorphic Forms</li>\n<li>Montgomery and Vaughan, Multiplicative Number Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-exponential","status":"resolved","id":"689fa138a0ce2d6c","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-exponential]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-exponential","status":"resolved","id":"689fa138a0ce2d6c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}$ is the uniquely specified complex exponential from [[58-df-exponential]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"N \\in \\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}","display":false},{"tex":"\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TrigSum}:\\omega\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{DistToInteger}:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trigonometric\\text{-}sum} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{TrigSum}(N,\\alpha)\\coloneqq\\sum_{n=1}^{N}\\exp(2\\pi i\\alpha n)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}distance\\text{-}to\\text{-}integer}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{DistToInteger}(\\alpha)\\coloneqq\\inf\\{|\\alpha-m|:m\\in\\mathbb Z\\}","display":true},{"tex":"N=0","display":false},{"tex":"0","display":false},{"tex":"G(a, q) = \\sum_{n=1}^q e^{2\\pi i a n^2/q}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{DistToInteger}(\\alpha)","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha","display":false},{"tex":"N^{1/2+\\epsilon}","display":false}],"bytes":1842,"backlinks":[{"id":"b704bd521f4cdc1f","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1326","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-trigonometric-sum.md|58-df-trigonometric-sum]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["689fa138a0ce2d6c"]}